 ## Background
-Originated from the 3D Gaussian Splatting paper by Kerbl et al. (2023) [S1, unofficial][S3][S5, S10, unofficial]. The method was developed to enable real-time differentiable rendering of 3D scenes represented as Gaussian splats. It builds on the tile-based rasterization techniques used in traditional graphics pipelines but adapts them for the specific needs of Gaussian splatting, including conic matrix approximation and alpha blending. The implementation is typically provided as a custom PyTorch autograd function wrapping a C++/CUDA backend [S2, unofficial][S3][S4, S10, unofficial].
